/**
 * Outfit, compiled into the source rather than read from disk.
 *
 * THIS IS NOT PREMATURE. It is the fix for a 500 that three separate local
 * checks all passed, and the fault is worth stating because it is a trap any
 * bundled runtime sets:
 *
 * readingPdf.mjs resolved its fonts with `new URL("./fonts/", import.meta.url)`,
 * which is correct in the repo -- the file sits at netlify/lib/readingPdf.mjs
 * and the fonts at netlify/lib/fonts/. esbuild then inlines that module INTO
 * netlify/functions/pdf.mjs, so at runtime `import.meta.url` names a different
 * directory and `./fonts/` resolves to netlify/functions/fonts/, which does not
 * exist. The path is right in the source and wrong in the artefact.
 *
 * `included_files` shipped the fonts correctly; nothing could find them.
 *
 * A base64 constant has no path to get wrong. It cannot be moved by a bundler,
 * it needs no included_files entry, and it fails at build time rather than on
 * somebody's download if it is ever missing. 110 KB of source for a class of
 * failure that is otherwise invisible until a paying customer clicks a button.
 *
 * REGENERATE with tools/build-fonts.mjs if the font is ever updated.
 *
 * Outfit is SIL Open Font License 1.1, which permits embedding and
 * redistribution. github.com/googlefonts/outfit
 */

/** Weight 400 -- the gate numerals. */
export const OUTFIT_400 = Buffer.from(
  "",
  "base64",
);

/** Weight 600 -- the centre names, and every heading in the document. */
export const OUTFIT_600 = Buffer.from(
  "",
  "base64",
);
